#
# We keep the time loop over t sequential to preserve the natural temporal
# dependency of the FDTD scheme. Inside each time-step, however, each
# spatial loop writes to distinct array elements, so we can safely
# parallelize them with OpenMP via Exo's `parallelize_loop` primitive.
#
# The layout ex[nx, ny], ey[nx, ny], hz[nx, ny] is row-major in C, so j is
# the innermost stride-1 index. We parallelize over i (rows) so that each
# thread processes full contiguous j-ranges, which is cache- and
# vectorization-friendly.
